      "examples": {
        "openers": [
          {
            "post": "2026-07-02-the-quarterly-tech-checkup",
            "text": "You set up your mom's phone. You installed the right apps, hid the confusing ones, configured the accessibility settings. You walked her through the emergency gestures and laminated a cheat sheet for her fridge. You did everything right."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-09-25-essential-home-automation-older-parents-practical-low-cost-setup-guide",
            "text": "My mum kept leaving the iron on."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-07-14-best-tablets-for-seniors-2026",
            "text": "I tested six tablets with five different grandparents over six weeks. I watched them try to make video calls, send messages, look at photos, and read the news. I watched them succeed, fail, get frustrated, and (in two cases) put the tablet down and never pick it up again."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-07-01-best-phones-for-seniors-2026",
            "text": "When my mom lost $4,200 to a fake Microsoft scam and I built her a simple phone app called Buddy, I realized the phone she was using mattered almost as much as the apps she had on it."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-06-27-best-free-phone-apps-seniors",
            "text": "For six months, every app I recommended to my mom went through the same brutal evaluation process: she used it for a week, then either kept using it or deleted it. No exceptions."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-10-05-local-llms-as-system-tooling-running-sub-3b-models",
            "text": "You need an AI assistant that runs on your own machine. The cloud options are good but they are not yours. You want something that actually does things — reads your screen, controls your smart home, answers questions in Finnish or English, and never sends your data to a server you don't control."
          }
        ],
        "closers": [
          {
            "post": "2026-07-02-the-quarterly-tech-checkup",
            "text": "Want a printable version? I made a {{< aff merchant=\"ko-fi\" text=\"Senior Phone Setup & Maintenance Checklist\" url=\"https://ko-fi.com/s/a567718347\" >}} that covers all four posts in one place — initial setup, quarterly checkup steps, and the emergency playbook. Laminate it, keep i"
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-09-25-essential-home-automation-older-parents-practical-low-cost-setup-guide",
            "text": "That's it. That's the whole system."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-07-14-best-tablets-for-seniors-2026",
            "text": "Buy the iPad 10th gen. Spend the $100-200 savings vs. an iPad Pro on a nice case and a long Apple Care+ warranty. For dementia or extreme low-tech-comfort, GrandPad is worth the $720/year."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-07-01-best-phones-for-seniors-2026",
            "text": "{{< aff-disclosure-inline >}}"
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-06-27-best-free-phone-apps-seniors",
            "text": "Together, those three pieces — the app, the setup, and the conversation — prevent 90% of the support calls and most of the heartbreak."
          },
          {
            "post": "2026-10-05-local-llms-as-system-tooling-running-sub-3b-models",
            "text": "Whatever you choose, take 30 minutes on a Saturday to set it up properly. The local LLM is the second-most-important thing; the setup is the first. A senior with a well-set-up local AI will be happier than a senior with a poorly-set-up flagship cloud service."
          }
        ],
